# Doc entries a pull request removes on purpose, one per line: "function <name>"
# or "tag <name>". CI compares a pull request's regenerated docs with its base
# (.github/workflows/ci.yml, docs-reproducible) and refuses every entry lost, or
# fallen back to a lower source, that is not listed here. List an entry only
# when the engine no longer has it; an upstream that merely stopped publishing
# one belongs in docs/retained instead. A trailing "# reason" is fine. CI fails
# on a line it cannot read, on "1", and on an entry the pull request does not
# actually remove: so clear an entry in the next pull request after it merges.
